35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The roads closed, yet the halls stayed open. And forty visitors per session? That is a strong signal we cannot ignore.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The bus data is stark. An hour’s round trip to a staffed counter. That isolation is the real barrier we must address.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the volunteer list shows retired tradespeople, but nobody on payroll can supervise them! That’s a huge gap.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant covers year one, then the flat budget absorbs the shock. The vehicle line overran by a third. Structural leaks, not size issues.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,The technician who certified our power tools retired in spring. We lack the internal expertise to manage new technical programs safely.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, those forty visitors prove people will come if we go to them. The roads closing did not stop the community halls, so a mobile service could be resilient.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the halls stayed open, but our remote catalogue peaks after nine. We are missing the people who cannot travel, not just those who cannot drive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, the old digitisation project failed because nobody finished it! We keep judging new ideas by how they sound, ignoring that similar shapes already left messy records here.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the ledger confirms the vehicle line overran by a third. If we choose the mobile option, we are betting on a budget that already leaks.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the associations train their own staff, but we lack certified supervisors. We cannot outsource safety checks to unvetted volunteers.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle costs worry me, but the attendance proves the need. Perhaps we can find a way to make it sustainable?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the evening data shows demand peaks after we lock up. A mobile unit could reach those isolated residents without forcing them to travel.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, wait! The retired tradespeople are already running the repair clinic. We have the skills, we just need to trust them!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, trust is not a budget line. The grant expires, the flat budget absorbs the shock, and the vehicle costs keep climbing. That is the trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the register confirms no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators. We cannot rely on unvetted volunteers for safety-critical roles.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I hear your caution. But the halls proved resilience when roads closed. We must find a path that respects both the need and the budget.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the isolation is the problem. If we don’t reach them, the service fails before it starts.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, but the evening groups still meet! They didn’t need a budget to keep going. Why do we think new ideas need more money than they actually do?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, those groups are volunteer-run, not budgeted. I’m looking at the county grant terms. Year one is paid, year two is a flat budget shock.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the evening groups are a different model. We lack the internal supervision structure to replicate that success safely without new training.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
